From 36478cd54ed736e01f4ad3c1519ca5ac85260c3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:56:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 165/166] hw/misc: add spinel-ncp, an OpenThread NCP's SPI port
 on a chardev

OpenThread's network co-processor on SPI (ncp_spi.cpp): each transaction
carries a 5-byte header each way (flag with the reset bit, accept and
data lengths) and a frame passes when the transaction carries it and the
other side accepts that many bytes. The interrupt is low while a frame
or the reset header waits. The spinel application lives behind a
chardev, which carries whole frames, nRESET and nWAKE.

nWAKE held low through a reset starts Nest's SPI bootloader, which
zb-loader drives to flash new NCP firmware. The model then switches the
port to raw mode: MOSI goes out byte by byte (zb-loader keeps the chip
selected after a command and waits for the interrupt), the next
transaction clocks out the queued reply from its first byte, and the
interrupt is low while a reply waits.
